  Hand-written test fixture for Novox's MusicXML importer (MIT, like the engine), laid out like
  Dorico 5/6 exports in published samples: a bare measure-level <sound tempo> beside a separate
  <direction> holding the metronome mark, <lyric number="N" placement="below"> with verse
  numbers out of order and <extend/>, and <sound dacapo/fine> written as measure-level elements
  (D.C. at the start of its measure) in the top part only. Not taken from a sample, so
  unverified for Dorico: the <elision> between two <text> elements, the cue notes, a second
  voice that stops short without a <forward>, a metronome mark with no <sound> (a tempo change
  read from the mark alone), and the transposing bass clarinet's <transpose>.

  Played out: m1-m6 (verse 1), D.C. to m1-m2 (verse 2), Fine.
-->
